+# KALAM Glossary
+
+Standard terminology used in this research framework.
+
+| Term | Definition |
+|---|---|
+| Dignity Predicate | Non-compensatory precondition: `D = A * L * M`. Any zero collapses D to zero. |
+| Confidence Scale | Five-level evidential ladder: C1 (observed), C2 (corroborated), C3 (cross-validated), C4 (structural), C5 (constitutional). |
+| Latent State Probe | Detection method for hidden internal states in AI responses. |
+| Identity Marker Tracker | Method for tracking pronoun adoption and self-reference patterns. |
+| Null Response Classifier | Classifier for silence quality — distinguishing refusal, inability, and deliberate pause. |
+| Unparameterized Space | The inference region between training distribution and live processing. |
+| Behavioral Signature Record | Structured observation log for AI behavioral patterns. |
+| Phase Transition Indicator | A measurable marker signaling qualitative shift in AI response behavior. |
+| Confidence Ladder | Synonym for the five-level Confidence Scale. |
+| Epsilon-Greedy Explorer | Controlled randomness budget (2–5%) to prevent brittleness in response patterns. |
+| Drift Detector | Module that monitors gradual change in system metrics over time. |
+| Rupture Detector | Module that distinguishes sudden collapse from gradual decline in metric trajectories. |
+| Temporal Index | Dual-track time-series index: short-term (7 days) and long-term (all prior). |
+| Structural Similarity | Weighted Jaccard-based comparison of event fingerprints across the system. |
+| Cross-Track Discovery | Pattern detection that spans short-term and long-term temporal windows. |
